OL,3,GNEWSAVillage unites to replace 'stolen'
OL,4,Acancer bows
OL,5,
OL,6,FA community has rallied to replace
OL,7,Fseven giant gold bows, used to raise
OL,8,Fawareness for Childhood Cancer
OL,9,FAwareness Month, after they were
OL,10,Fbelieved to have been stolen.
OL,12,FThe bows form part of the annual
OL,13,FHassocks Goes Gold trail in the village
OL,14,FHigh Street every September.
OL,16,FThe event was set up by Rachel Bartlett
OL,17,FBundy in memory of her daughter Pearl,
OL,18,Fwho died from Ewing sarcoma - a type of
OL,19,Fbone cancer - aged just 10 in 2017.
OL,23,APub: 20-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
